<title>CHINA: China's Jan-Nov edible oil buying detailed.</title>
<headline>China's Jan-Nov edible oil buying detailed.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following table shows the three edible oil import figures of five major Chinese customs offices as well as the country of origin from January to November 1996.</p>
<p>Details were provided by the General Administration of Customs of China.</p>
<p>Figures are in tonnes. Percentages represent the share of the total market. Percentages may not add up to 100 percent as details of some smaller import regions and supplying countries have not been included.</p>
<p>SOYOIL</p>
<p>    Nov imports  55,960    Jan-Nov total imports  1,203,978</p>
<p> CUSTOMS	     Nov	 Pct	   Jan-Nov	 Pct</p>
<p>    Shanghai	    30	 0.05	  172,575	14.3</p>
<p>    Qingdao	     37	 0.07	  133,727	11.1</p>
<p>    Tianjin	 29,500	52.7	   231,301	19.2</p>
<p>    Nanjing		0	 0.0	   127,600	10.6</p>
<p>    Jiulong	  5,034	 9.0	    80,343	 6.7</p>
<p>(Shenzhen) ORIGINS</p>
<p>    Brazil	  36,740	65.7	   916,735	76.1</p>
<p>    Argentina     17,000	30.3	   152,203	12.6</p>
<p>    U.S.		  10	 0.02	   30,739	 2.6</p>
<p>    Malaysia	   500	 0.9	    25,752	 2.1</p>
<p>PALM OIL</p>
